# Social Explorer

A social media research platform: SvelteKit 2 / Svelte 5 web app and API (`ex-accell-ui/`), Python
ETL (`etl/`), a radio ingestion service (`wavepulse/`), a Jupyter image (`jupyter/`) and a
VitePress docs site (`docs-site/`), around PostgreSQL with `pg_duckdb`.

**Read `AGENTS.md` first.** It is the source of truth. If this file and `AGENTS.md` disagree,
`AGENTS.md` wins and this file is the bug.

## Rules that are easy to break

- **Collected content stays out.** No real post, handle, transcript or user data in a prompt, log,
  test, fixture, issue or PR. Tests use the synthetic demo generator.
- **Secrets stay out.** No `.env*` (except `.env.example`), keys or tokens in a commit or a prompt.
  Never reference `DEPLOY_SSH_KEY`, `SCW_*` or `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` from new code.
- **Auth first.** Every `/api/*` route needs a session unless `guard.ts` lists it as public; code
  execution and user management are admin-only. SQL is parameterised; no shell from user input.
- **Do not touch deployment.** `deploy.yml` publishes to production and is for humans only.
- **Schema changes are new migrations** in `ex-accell-ui/db/migrations/`, never edits to an
  applied one.
- **Coverage only goes up.** Do not lower `coverage.thresholds` in `vitest.config.ts`.

## Deliverables, hard stops and labels

Every task ends in a pull request, a written finding or a `no_work_needed` verdict with evidence;
if blocked or out of scope, write an evidenced finding instead of stopping silent. Never merge or
push to `main`, or remove `hold`, `do-not-merge`, `needs-human` or `human-queue`. Stop and write a
finding before auth, secrets or supply-chain changes, new dependencies or outbound destinations.
Only `issue-approved` issues (with acceptance criteria) are agent work; never `human-queue`.

## Branches and checks

Never push to `main`. Branch, open a pull request, and wait for the `ci` check (the aggregate job
in `.github/workflows/test.yml`). Report what the commands in `AGENTS.md` printed before you call a
change done.
